<title>UK: Rolls Royce rebounds, Lehman targets 250p.</title>
<headline>Rolls Royce rebounds, Lehman targets 250p.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Rolls-Royce Plc rebounded on Tuesday in active trading amid perceptions the shares had fallen too far in recent weeks, dealers said.</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers analyst Charles Armitage said he believed the stock had reached to bottom of its trading range and was targeting the 250p level.</p>
<p>By 0914 GMT, the shares were up 7p, or 3.25 percent, at 223p.</p>
</text>
